# F1: the FINAL-STEP DRAM HOLD NEGATIVE CONTROL on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-levern-final-hold-time-gate (the timed interleaved arm plus QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_FAULT=final-hold). While a decoder runs, the first partial prefill whose next step is its final one (the step that builds the
# engine) is held ONCE as if the DRAM predicate refused it: a decode step runs instead ("lever N final-step dram hold ... fault:final-hold", then a step line with reason=final-dram), and the final step then goes through.
# Tests: warmup, a decoder finishing mid-prefill, and the busy boundary prompts. READ: exactly one hold line, the prompt completes with the SAME hashes as A1's levern_equal_busy rows and the arrival of H1's shape,
# nothing left held (the next request completes), c2_smoke_check clean. Duration (estimate): 60 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/lever-n four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lever-n and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lever-n-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/lever-n commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lever-n-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-levern-final-hold-time-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,levern_decoder_finishes,levern_equal_busy
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=fault-injection arm: its test list is fixed by the pack protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
